  "releaseNotes": "v2.0.0 — Breaking Changes and Modernization:\n\t\t\t- BREAKING: Dropped net6.0 and net7.0 target frameworks; now targeting net8.0, net9.0, and net10.0\n\t\t\t- BREAKING: IEventHandler.Handle now requires CancellationToken as mandatory parameter (no longer optional overload)\n\t\t\t- BREAKING: EventMapService moved from EventFlux namespace to EventFlux.Services namespace\n\t\t\t- BREAKING: CreateScopePerEvent default changed from true to false (ambient scope by default)\n\t\t\t- Modernized TimeoutBehavior to use WaitAsync for reliable cancellation on all supported TFMs\n\t\t\t- Distinguished caller cancellation from timeout in TimeoutBehavior (no longer logs false timeout warnings)\n\t\t\t- Hot-path LINQ and allocation optimizations (Span-based, array-backed, allocation-free dispatch)\n\t\t\t- Eliminated all nullable warnings and fixed NullReferenceException in parameterless EventService/EventMapService constructors",
